    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n16 South View is a well-presented three-bedroom terraced home, ideally located on the highly sought-after Ballinlough Road. Combining convenience, generous living space, and excellent potential, this property offers a superb opportunity for purchasers seeking to create a stylish home in a prime urban setting.\n\nGround floor accommodation consists of a bright, spacious open-plan kitchen/dining/living area, main bathroom, garden porch with utility space and a ground floor double bedroom.\n\nThe first floor is deceivingly spacious with two well-appointed double bedrooms to the front and rear of the home, one of which benefits from fitted wardrobes. There is also a second bathroom on this level.\n\nTo the rear, the private garden has been superbly maintained by its current owners over the years finished with split-level patio spaces, mature shrubbery and flower beds. The garden shed offers a convenient storage space for all gardening needs. There is also direct gated access onto the rear laneway behind the South View terrace. On-street parking is readily available to the front of the home.\n\nBallinlough is a highly desired area being minutes away from the city centre where all social and essential amenities are within easy reach. There are excellent schools nearby, plus it is within short proximity to The South Link Road making areas such as Douglas and Blackrock easily accessible.\n\nViewings come highly recommended to fully appreciate this well-appointed home in a fantastic central location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.30m x 0.93\nA welcoming entrance hall that provides access to the living accommodation and the ground floor double bedroom.\n\nKitchen/Dining/Living Area - 8.20m x 4.82m\nThe kitchen/dining/living area has an expansive floorplan with two Velux windows and a sliding door to the rear that make this a bright and inviting space. The kitchen consists of floor and eye level units with a peninsula island that cleverly separates the kitchen and living spaces. Ceramic tiled flooring and splashback finish the space to a very high standard.The main bathroom, garden porch and utility room can be accessed from this area with stairs that give access to further accommodation overhead. The space also features an open fireplace, wall mounted lighting and storage under the stairs.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.20m x 1.81m\nFully tiled bath suite that features an electric shower, recessed lighting, bidet and a vanity wash hand basin unit.\n\nGarden Porch - 1.55m x 3.78m\nBright space that features ceramic flooring, large windows and a sliding door with onto the rear garden. The utility room can also be accessed from this space.\n\nUtility Room - 1.55m x 1.62m\nShelved space with ceramic flooring and services for washing and drying machines.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.30m x 3.82m\nGround floor double bedroom with a fitted wardrobe, open fireplace and window onto the front of the home.\n\nLanding - 1.75m x 1.29m\nLanding area gives access to two double bedrooms and a bathroom.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.20m x 3.82m\nLocated to the rear of the home, this double bedroom is finished with solid oak flooring and benefits from a large window onto the rear garden.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.18m x 3.72m\nGenerous sized double bedroom that benefits from a large window to the front of the home and a fitted wardrobe.\n\nFirst Floor Bathroom - 2.32m x 1.18m\nTastefully finished fully tiled three-piece shower suite with a feature vanity wash hand basin unit and a lighted mirror.\n\n"
      },
